  "Number": 38,
  "Question": "If \\(f(a)=a-2\\) and \\(F(a,b)=b^2+a,\\) then \\(F[3,f(4)]\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a^2-4a+7\\)",
    "B": "\\(28\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(11\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First evaluate \\(f(4)\\), since its value becomes the second input of \\(F\\):\n\\[\nf(4)=4-2=2.\n\\]\nIn \\(F(a,b)=b^2+a\\), the second input is squared and the first input is added. Therefore\n\\[\nF[3,f(4)]=F(3,2)=2^2+3=7.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(7\\), choice C.",
